# Copy to `.env` for local API (never commit `.env`). The API loads it via dotenv (`server.js`).
# After filling SMTP_*, run: npm run email:test
# On Vercel: Project → Settings → Environment Variables (same names; no .env file).

# --- Email: Gmail (use an App Password, not your normal Gmail password) ---
# 1. Google Account → Security → 2-Step Verification ON
# 2. Security → App passwords → create "Mail" → copy the 16-character password
# 3. Fill SMTP_USER / SMTP_PASS / SMTP_FROM with your Gmail address
SMTP_SERVICE=gmail
SMTP_USER=youraddress@gmail.com
SMTP_PASS=xxxx xxxx xxxx xxxx
SMTP_FROM=youraddress@gmail.com

# Optional: link in emails (Open calendar button)
# APP_URL=http://localhost:5173

# --- Microsoft Teams / Outlook calendar sync (recommended for cancel to work) ---
# Email ICS cancel is often ignored when sending via Gmail SMTP into Microsoft 365.
# Create an Azure AD app (application permissions): Calendars.ReadWrite — admin consent.
# Then set these on Vercel / .env so PMO can create, update, and remove events on assignee calendars:
# MS_GRAPH_TENANT_ID=xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx
# MS_GRAPH_CLIENT_ID=xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx
# MS_GRAPH_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret

# --- Email: other SMTP (omit SMTP_SERVICE=gmail and use these instead) ---
# Prefer smtp.office365.com if your org uses Microsoft 365 (better Teams calendar processing than Gmail):
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.office365.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_SECURE=false
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASS=
# SMTP_FROM=noreply@yourdomain.com

# --- Database (production) ---
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# Database password (Settings → Database) — used by npm run db:migrate or POST /api/admin/db/apply-schema
# SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD=your-database-password
# Optional pooler host if not ap-southeast-1: SUPABASE_DB_HOST=aws-0-ap-southeast-1.pooler.supabase.com
# Or full URI: SUPABASE_DB_URL=postgresql://postgres.[ref]:[PASSWORD]@aws-0-[region].pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# --- Local dev only (file-backed store; not for production) ---
# ALLOW_LOCAL_STORE=1
